Example 14.1 : A progressive harmonic wave is given by y = 10^{-4} \sin(100\pi t - 0.1\pi x). Calculate its (i) frequency, (ii) wavelength and (iii) velocity y and x are in metre.
Solution: comparing with the standard equation of progressive wave
y = A \sin\left(\frac{2\pi t}{T} - \frac{2\pi x}{\lambda}\right)

Oscillations and Waves
