=\lambda \frac{(v-v_s)}{v}
=\lambda \left(1-\frac{v_s}{v}\right)
On rearranging terms, we can write
\frac{\lambda' - \lambda}{\lambda} = -\frac{v_s}{v}
or
\frac{\Delta \lambda}{\lambda} = \frac{v_s}{v_s}
we are told that \frac{\Delta \lambda}{\lambda} = 0.032/100. And since v = c = 3 \times 10^8 \text{ ms}^{-1}, we get
v_s = v \frac{\Delta \lambda}{\lambda} = -(3 \times 10^8 \,\text{ms}^{-1} \times 0.032/100) = -9.6 \times 10^4 \,\text{ms}^{-1}.
The negative sign shows that the star is receding away. This made the astrophysists to conclude that the world is in a state of expansion
